    "transcript": "Jade: I'm at the ticket hall. Are you waiting on platform six?\nOwen: No. The announcement has changed our platform to eight. I'm standing beside the stairs.\nJade: Is our express train still leaving at ten thirty?\nOwen: It is running fifteen minutes late. The display now says ten forty-five.\nJade: Then we will miss our connection at North Junction. Shall we use a direct service instead?\nOwen: Yes. The conductor says the eleven o'clock service goes directly to the coast. We won't need a transfer.\nJade: Is our ticket valid on that service?\nOwen: Yes, but our seat reservation is not. We can ask for new seats at the desk.\nJade: I'd like a seat near the luggage space. This suitcase is heavy.\nOwen: There are two seats together in carriage five. The fare is the same, so we don't need to pay extra.\nJade: Good. What is the new arrival time?\nOwen: Twelve ten. I'll message our friend now. She is meeting us outside the station.\nJade: Thanks. I'm buying some water before we board. Do you want anything?\nOwen: Just water. Please meet me by the stairs at ten fifty. We should allow ten minutes to get to the right carriage.\nJade: All right. I'll check the platform display again before I come.",
